  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strenghtened labour market information for evidence based policy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sri Lanka&#x2019;s progress toward decent work is limited by fragmented data systems, uneven statistical capacity, and weak coordination across institutions responsible for labour-market governance. Dispersed and infrequently updated administrative datasets hinder policymakers&#x2019; ability to identify trends, forecast labour demand, and respond to vulnerabilities. Strengthening labour-market information and research coherence is therefore critical for evidence-based decision-making. 

Reliable data enables targeted policies to address informality, youth unemployment, gender disparities, sectoral mismatches, and regional inequalities, while supporting skills development, labour standards monitoring, and social-protection reform. To this end, Sri Lanka will establish a national Labour Market Information and Analysis Portal integrating data from key institutions, complemented by regular research and policy briefs from the National Institute of Labour Studies and other research organizations. These measures will enhance analytical capacity, inform inclusive and forward-looking policies, and ensure interventions are grounded in robust evidence.</narrative>
  </description>
